# Pairs with RAllOrNothing. The receiver hands a tree to the cross-tree barrier
# in the wrong order: it notifies the barrier first and registers the
# delegation afterwards. LatticeGrain.ReplicationApply states the ordering as
# never reversible, and this is why: once the barrier has decided on the other
# tree's notify, that tree is finalised and serves the saga post-saga, while
# this tree has neither a delegation nor a local decision, so its registry
# answers InFlight and the gate serves its key pre-saga.
MODULE: RAllOrNothingNotifyBeforeRegister
TARGET: RAllOrNothing
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a cross-tree receiver notifies the barrier before it registers the delegation, so a sibling can finalise while this tree reads InFlight
PERTURBS: DeliverTerminal, ReceiverRegister, ReceiverNotify

--- FIND
                  /\ rstage' = IF rstage[tr] = "idle" THEN [rstage EXCEPT ![tr] = "register"] ELSE rstage
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the hand-off starts with the notify.
                  /\ rstage' = IF rstage[tr] = "idle" THEN [rstage EXCEPT ![tr] = "notify"] ELSE rstage
--- END
--- FIND
    /\ rstage' = [rstage EXCEPT ![tr] = "notify"]
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: registration is the last step.
    /\ rstage' = [rstage EXCEPT ![tr] = "done"]
--- END
--- FIND
    /\ rstage' = [rstage EXCEPT ![tr] = "done"]
    /\ UNCHANGED <<originVars, xtree, netVars, leafVars, rarr, rexp, rdec, rout, rdeleg, rdial, rtodo,
                   gone, purged, ptrim, rs, detached, rpoison, losses, preguard, filt, verdict, afence, ubnd, decom, afresh,
                   boff, bpur, bfence, bcaught, acaught, abnd, uimp, xo, xs, bclr, bdrop, dw, bfresh>>
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the notify is followed by the registration.
    /\ rstage' = [rstage EXCEPT ![tr] = "register"]
    /\ UNCHANGED <<originVars, xtree, netVars, leafVars, rarr, rexp, rdec, rout, rdeleg, rdial, rtodo,
                   gone, purged, ptrim, rs, detached, rpoison, losses, preguard, filt, verdict, afence, ubnd, decom, afresh,
                   boff, bpur, bfence, bcaught, acaught, abnd, uimp, xo, xs, bclr, bdrop, dw, bfresh>>
--- END
